1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,000
Most study apps stop at the right answer — this one starts from what you can teach.

2
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:06,200
Airplane mode on — the whole loop still runs.

3
00:00:06,200 --> 00:00:09,270
No LLM, no cloud — nothing a student writes leaves the device.

4
00:00:09,270 --> 00:00:14,270
A middle-school science app where students teach an AI companion.

5
00:00:14,270 --> 00:00:18,270
Your turn to teach — the textbook is hidden while you explain.

6
00:00:18,270 --> 00:00:26,270
{\an8}On-device check: did the key ideas make it into your explanation?

7
00:00:26,270 --> 00:00:36,270
{\an8}Miss them and he asks for more — no points lost, just another try.

8
00:00:39,270 --> 00:00:46,270
{\an8}The key terms he caught, chip by chip.

9
00:00:46,270 --> 00:00:50,770
{\an8}Then he asks a cataloged follow-up — never a free-form chat.

10
00:00:50,770 --> 00:00:55,270
Pick the answer that matches what he believes…

11
00:00:55,270 --> 00:01:01,270
A miss costs a heart, records the gap, and triggers a hint — never the answer.

12
00:01:01,270 --> 00:01:06,770
{\an8}Re-explain with the hint — same method, second try.

13
00:01:06,770 --> 00:01:16,270
{\an8}Compare it against the textbook yourself.

14
00:01:16,270 --> 00:01:24,970
Only progress is recorded — the explanation itself is never stored.

15
00:01:24,970 --> 00:01:31,000
{\an8}The miss you just saw is already on his karte.

16
00:01:31,000 --> 00:01:36,770
{\an8}All 29 — cataloged from real classroom surveys.

17
00:01:36,770 --> 00:01:45,770
{\an8}Plus perk: a parent-ready report of what your teaching fixed.

18
00:01:45,770 --> 00:01:57,770
{\an8}Plus via RevenueCat — store unreachable, so buying stays blocked.
